  <div class="wrap trust-strip__inner">
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">★</span><div><strong>Trustpilot 4.7+</strong><span>Customer rating</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">PPAI</span><div><strong>PPAI Member</strong><span>Promotional products industry</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">S</span><div><strong>Shopify Partner</strong><span>Commerce experience</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section> -->


<section class="sec" id="details">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">What it does</span><h2>Built around the supplier workflow.</h2><p class="lead">Keep the technology behind the scenes and make the outcome easy for your team to understand.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>PO receiving</h3><p>Receive the approved purchase order from the buyer’s procurement system.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>Transaction matching</h3><p>Connect the PO back to the original PunchOut session and returned cart.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>Validation</h3><p>Check key order details before creating the commerce order.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">04</span><h3>Shopify order creation</h3><p>Create the matching Shopify order only after the approved PO arrives.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">05</span><h3>Duplicate protection</h3><p>Use idempotent transaction handling to reduce duplicate order risk.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">06</span><h3>Status visibility</h3><p>See whether the PO was received, validated and converted successfully.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="workflow">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">How it works</span><h2>A simple path from buyer request to result.</h2><p class="lead">The platform keeps each step connected.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps"><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>Cart returns</h3><p>The buyer finishes shopping and sends the cart back to procurement.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>Buyer approves</h3><p>Their internal requisition and approval process happens in procurement.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>PO arrives</h3><p>PunchOut Central receives the approved purchase order.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>Order is created</h3><p>The matching Shopify order is created automatically.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="proof">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Built for trust</span><h2>Proven enough for the customer you cannot afford to lose.</h2><p class="lead">Simple on the surface. Dependable underneath.</p></div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>90+</strong><span>customers use PunchOut technology built by our team.</span></article>
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>$50M+</strong><span>in order value processed through our technology every year.</span></article>
      <article class="metric metric--dark reveal"><strong>cXML + OCI</strong><span>Buyer sessions, carts, POs, store orders and invoices stay connected and visible.</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Keep exploring</span><h2>Explore the platform</h2></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/punchout/"><span>Platform</span><h3>PunchOut</h3><p>See how the buyer starts the procurement-to-commerce journey.</p><b>Explore →</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/invoices/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Invoices</h3><p>Keep invoicing connected to the PO and store order.</p><b>Explore →</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/transactions/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Transactions</h3><p>See PO and order status from one place.</p><b>Explore →</b></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Questions suppliers usually ask</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>When is the Shopify order created?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>After the approved purchase order is received, not when the PunchOut cart is returned.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can PunchOut Central match the PO to the original session?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. The platform is designed to keep the gateway, session, cart, PO and ecommerce order correlated.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>What if a PO is sent twice?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>The architecture includes duplicate and idempotency controls to reduce duplicate order creation.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-cta">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <span class="ey">A bigger opportunity is waiting</span>
    <h2>When the buyer asks for PunchOut, say yes.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Start with your first enterprise buyer and grow from there.</p>
    <div class="page-hero__actions">
      <a class="btn pri" href="https://app.punchoutcentral.com/platform/register" target="_blank">Connect my first buyer →</a>
      <a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
